We need to propose retrosynthesis route using given templates in order: ['29646', '1914389', '1914390', '149040', '1914391'].

We need to construct JSON tree: root is target molecule (type mol, smiles target). Then children: reaction nodes each with template_id and children precursors (type mol). Since we need at least 5 reactions, we will have 5 reaction steps sequentially, each reaction node's children are precursors, and one of those precursors is the product of previous step? Actually retrosynthesis tree: root target, then first reaction (template 29646) splits into precursors; then each precursor may be further broken by next reaction etc. Since we need exactly 5 reactions in order, we can make a linear chain: each reaction takes the previous product as a precursor and generates a simpler precursor, until we reach simple buyable molecules (we don't need to verify buyable). So we need to apply each template to the molecule to get precursors. We need to know what each template does. We can try to apply them using apply_template tool to see outcomes.

Let's start by checking target SMILES: O[C@H]1C[C@@H](O[C@@H]([C@@H]1C)/C=C(CO)/C)C/C=C/C=C/C(O)=O

We need to apply template 29646. Use check_smiles_reaction_template_matching to see if applicable.
{
    "tool_name": "check_smiles_reaction_template_matching",
    "arguments": {
        "smiles": "O[C@H]1C[C@@H](O[C@@H]([C@@H]1C)/C=C(CO)/C)C/C=C/C=C/C(O)=O",
        "template_id": "29646"
    }
}
